<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<TcPlcObject Version="1.1.0.1">
  <POU Name="F_SetBeamParams" Id="{a4b27d6a-ec21-4812-9b64-4caff94fb4ba}" SpecialFunc="None">
    <Declaration><![CDATA[(*
    F_SetBeamParams - builds a beam-parameter set from explicit values, with
    the PMPS limits applied to it.

    PURPOSE
        Packs the five beam-defining quantities a caller knows - requested
        transmission, photon-energy range mask, pulse rate, beam-class range
        mask and the auxiliary attenuator state - into one ST_BeamParams, and
        clamps the three quantities that have a physical limit:
            nTran     LIMIT(0, nTran, PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR)
            nRate     MIN(nRate, 1000000)   -> at most 1 000 000 Hz
            nBCRange  MIN(nBCRange, 32767)  -> at most 16#7FFF
        neVRange and astAuxAtt are copied unchanged. The set is returned by
        value; nothing here is written to a PMPS global.

    USAGE
        Call positionally, in declaration order, and use the returned set
        directly or hand it to a comparison or arbitration:
            stRequested := F_SetBeamParams(Tran, EvMask, Rate, BCRange, AuxAtt);
        The function keeps no state and has no side effects, so it may be
        called from any task, from production code and from test code. In this
        library it is used by the TcUnit suites (for example
        FB_SafeBPCompare_Test) to mint the beam-parameter sets they compare,
        which keeps the clamps identical between the tests and production.
        Only the constants PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR and
        PMPS_GVL.AUX_ATTENUATORS are read.

    OBJECTIVES
        - Give every source of a beam-parameter set (EPICS, JSON configuration,
          test fixtures) one place where the same clamps are applied, so a
          value that arrives by another route cannot skip them.
        - Keep the clamps on the side of less beam: a transmission above the
          scaling factor, a rate above 1 MHz or a beam-class mask above
          16#7FFF is reduced, never passed through.
        - Stay a pure function - no state, no side effects - so it is safe to
          call from a test assertion.

    UNITS AND VALID RANGES
        nTran     Transmission as a fraction of PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR
                  (currently REAL#1.0), so 0.5 means 50 % transmission.
                  Valid input 0 .. TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR. Clamped with LIMIT,
                  so a negative input becomes 0 (no transmission) and an input
                  above TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR becomes TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR
                  (100 %).
        neVRange  Bitmask of allowed photon-energy ranges, one bit per range;
                  16#FFFF_FFFF = every range, 0 = no range allowed. Unitless.
                  Not validated and not clamped - copied as received.
        nRate     Pulse rate in Hz. Valid input 0 .. 1 000 000 Hz (1 MHz, the
                  maximum LCLS-II rate); 0 Hz means no beam. Clamped from above
                  only, so a value above 1 MHz is reduced to 1 MHz.
        nBCRange  Bitmask of allowed beam classes, one bit per beam class
                  (bit n = beam class n); 16#000F = classes 1..4, 0 = no class
                  allowed. Unitless. Clamped with MIN(..., 32767), i.e. to
                  16#7FFF: bit 15 (beam class 16, the PMPS fail-safe class)
                  and any higher bit is dropped from the mask.
        astAuxAtt Requested state of every auxiliary attenuator: 1-based array
                  of PMPS_GVL.AUX_ATTENUATORS entries (currently 16), each an
                  ST_PMPS_Attenuator with .nTran (transmission on the same
                  TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR scale, so 0.005 = 0.5 %) and .xAttOK
                  (attenuator status word - see the declaration comment).
                  Copied as received; the array bounds are fixed by the input
                  type and the entries are not validated.

    HISTORY
        2019-08-20 / Alex Wallace
            Function created (first real commit of this repository; earlier
            history is in pmps-dev). Transmission was then a percentage of
            "attenuation" in an input named fAtt.
        2020-07-07 / Alex Wallace
            Switched the library from attenuation percentage to transmission:
            the input became nTran and the clamp went through
            PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR.
        2021-04-20 / ghalym
            Dropped the per-pulse-energy input (fPP_mJ) and its 0..20 mJ clamp.
        2022-11-28 / ghalym
            Added the nBCRange beam-class range input.
        2023-01-09 / ghalym
            Added the 16#7FFF (32767) clamp on nBCRange.
        2026-11-28 / Scirix Agent
            Added this header and an inline comment for every declaration,
            including units and valid ranges; documentation only, no behaviour
            change (audit finding #259, convention conv_321640e095c0).

    NOTE
        - The fields this function does not take as arguments keep the
          ST_BeamParams type defaults in the returned set: aVetoDevices all
          FALSE (no stopper vetoes the beam), astApertures Width/Height 1E3 mm
          (apertures effectively wide open), neV 0, nBeamClass 0,
          nMachineMode 3, xValidToggle FALSE, xValid FALSE and nCohortInt 0.
          A caller that cares about stoppers, apertures or machine mode must
          set them on the result.
        - The clamps bound a value; they do not judge the set. Whether a set is
          acceptable for the beam that is actually running is decided further
          downstream, by F_SafeBPCompare / F_SafeBPCompare0Rate and the
          arbiter.
        - nTran is clamped with LIMIT but nRate and nBCRange with MIN, because
          UDINT and WORD cannot carry a negative value, so a lower bound on
          them would be dead code.
*)
FUNCTION F_SetBeamParams : ST_BeamParams
VAR_INPUT
    // Requested pre-optic transmission as a fraction of PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR (0 = no transmission, TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR = 100 %, so 0.5 = 50 %). Valid 0 .. TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR; clamped by LIMIT(0, nTran, TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR). Default 0 = no transmission.
    nTran    :    REAL := 0;
    // Photon-energy range mask, one bit per photon-energy range (unitless; 16#FFFF_FFFF = every range, 0 = no range allowed). Copied unchanged, not validated. Consumers AND masks, so an allowed set has to be a subset of the running one.
    neVRange    :    DWORD := 0;
    // Pulse rate in Hz, valid 0 .. 1 000 000 Hz (1 MHz = maximum LCLS-II rate); 0 Hz means no beam. Clamped from above with MIN(nRate, 1000000).
    nRate    :    UDINT := 0;
    // Beam-class range mask, one bit per beam class - bit n = beam class n (unitless; 16#000F = classes 1..4, 0 = no class allowed). Clamped with MIN(nBCRange, 32767) = 16#7FFF, which drops bit 15 (beam class 16, the fail-safe class) and any higher bit.
    nBCRange : WORD := 0;
    // Requested state of every auxiliary attenuator: 1-based, one entry per attenuator in PMPS_GVL.AUX_ATTENUATORS (currently 16). .nTran = transmission on the TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR scale (0.005 = 0.5 %), .xAttOK = attenuator status word (evaluated by F_AttenuatorOK: bit 0 AtTarget, bit 1 Moving, bit 2 LocalMode, bit 3 PMPSMode, bit 4 OK). Copied as received; the entries are not validated.
    astAuxAtt : ARRAY [1..PMPS_GVL.AUX_ATTENUATORS] OF ST_PMPS_Attenuator;
END_VAR
VAR
    // Working set that is filled from the inputs above and returned as the function result. The fields without an input keep their ST_BeamParams defaults - see the NOTE in the header.
    BeamParams    :    ST_BeamParams;

END_VAR
]]></Declaration>
    <Implementation>
      <ST><![CDATA[BeamParams.nTran := LIMIT(0,nTran,PMPS_GVL.TRANS_SCALING_FACTOR);
BeamParams.astAttenuators := astAuxAtt;
BeamParams.neVRange := neVRange;
BeamParams.nRate    := MIN(nRate,1000000);
BeamParams.nBCRange	:= MIN(nBCRange,32767);

F_SetBeamParams    := BeamParams;]]></ST>
    </Implementation>
  </POU>
</TcPlcObject>